{"id": "x00326", "text": "- `Fold.collect` works automatically through `apply` without changes to `returns/iterables.py`."}
{"id": "x00327", "text": "3. **Script Evaluation with Handle:**"}
{"id": "x00328", "text": "- **Open blocker (current focus)**: nested CSS selectors are not handled. For `<style>.a { .b { fill: red } } .c .d {…}</style>`, the collector serializes inner selector as `& .b`; `oxvg_ast::selectors::Selector::new(\"& .b\")` fails (`EmptySelector`), `\".a& .b\"` fails, `\":is(.a) .b\"` fails (`UnsupportedPseudoClassOrElement(\"is\")`), while plain `\".a .b\"` works. Root cause: oxvg's `selectors::parser::Parser` impl (in `oxvg_ast/src/selectors.rs`, only `Impl`/`Error`) leaves defaults `parse_is_and_where=false`, `parse_has=false`, `parse_parent_selector=false`; selectors 0.26.0 crate. Lightningcss `StyleRule` has `selectors`, `declarations`, `rules` (nested `CssRuleList`); `CssRule::Nesting(NestingRule)`/`NestedDeclarations` variants exist; `RelativeSelector` struct exists in selectors crate. Next step direction: expand nested selectors (join parent + `&`-relative) or enable parser features so implication works on full selectors."}
{"id": "x00329", "text": "- Passed `pnpm --filter drizzle-orm run test:types` (tsc cleanly passes!)."}
{"id": "x00330", "text": "- Specifically, if selector is `A > B`, matching `B` requires parent `A`. Both `A` and `B` are implicated."}
{"id": "x00331", "text": "- **Storage**: 4 embedded SQL migration files numbered 041 under `backend/resources/migrations/sqlite/` and `postgres/` (up+down), discoverable under `migrations/<provider>/041_*.sql` via `resources.FS`."}
{"id": "x00332", "text": "- Work on branch `feature/duration-sharding` from `main`."}
